        "term-type-facet-constraints.md",
        "implicit-vs-explicit-facets.md"
      ],
      "answer": "The pages give no FoodEx2 code for 'Bordsdruvor – färsk frukt' (table grapes, fresh fruit), so I can't give one. What they do support:\n- Food type: fresh fruit reads as a raw commodity. Choose a reportable, non-hierarchy raw base term and don't start from a hierarchy term (base-term-selection.md, RUNTIME_RULES.md). Check reportability in the intended hierarchy.\n- Facets: raw terms already carry F01 Source implicitly. Don't add F01 just to restate the commodity, and don't repeat implicit detail (term-type-facet-constraints.md, implicit-vs-explicit-facets.md).\n- Pesticide overlay: you've stated the pesticide domain, so it applies. Code the raw commodity as usual, then use the pesticide-valid candidate that maps to MATRIX. EFSA does the FoodEx2-to-MATRIX mapping downstream (pesticides-foodex2.md).\n- If the exact variety (table grape) isn't a valid pesticide-domain term, use the nearest valid generic candidate. Don't invent a code, and keep the extra detail in free text if the workflow allows (pesticides-foodex2.md). If the exact term is missing, the generic base plus F01 plus F26.A07XE is described in base-term-selection.md, but I can't confirm that fits here.\n- Validation: check reportability, deprecation and dismissal errors (BR08, BR20, BR21), which are blocking. An absent matrixCode or a PRIMo flag does not by itself show a term is invalid (pesticides-foodex2.md, base-term-selection.md).\n- The pages don't give grape-specific codes, and the Legal Limits database only covers raw, unprocessed samples (pesticides-foodex2.md).",
